Starting next year, residents of Connecticut will be able to add their driver's license or state ID to the Apple Wallet app on the iPhone and Apple Watch. The digital ID can be used to display proof of identity or age at TSA checkpoints in select airports, at select businesses, and in select iPhone apps, but acceptance is still very limited.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2024/04/apple-wallet-drivers-license-feature-iPhone-15-pro.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-947140" /><br/>
Last week, Connecticut <a href="https://portal.ct.gov/governor/news/press-releases/2026/11-2026/governor-lamont-and-connecticut-dmv-announce-launch-of-mobile-id">released a mobile ID app</a> on <a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/connecticut-mobile-id/id6757445743">iOS</a> and <a href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.idemia.mobileid.us.ct">Android</a>, and the app's developer IDEMIA <a href="https://na.idemia.com/ct-mid-about/ct-mid-troubleshooting-faqs/">said</a> Apple Wallet, Google Wallet, and Samsung Wallet support will be "coming soon." In a May 2026 press release, Connecticut Governor Ned Lamont's office <a href="https://portal.ct.gov/governor/news/press-releases/2026/05-2026/governor-lamont-and-the-state-bond-commission-approve-investments">said</a> it aimed to  support the trio of digital wallets "by August 2027."<br/>
<br/>
All the way back <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/2021/09/apple-announces-first-states-to-adopt-drivers-licenses-and-state-ids-in-wallet/">in September 2021</a>, Apple announced that Connecticut had "signed up" to offer driver's licenses and state IDs in the Apple Wallet app, but more than five years have passed and nothing has materialized. With a goal of August 2027 now in place, though, the functionality should finally be available next year.<br/>
<br/>
16 other U.S. states have rolled out Apple Wallet IDs so far: Arizona, Arkansas, California, Colorado, Georgia, Hawaii, Illinois, Iowa, Maryland, Montana, New Mexico, North Dakota, Ohio, Oklahoma, Virginia, and West Virginia. The feature is also available in Puerto Rico and works with Japan's My Number Card.<br/>
<br/>
Apple has also been preparing for the feature to go live <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/17/apple-wallet-ids-expanding-to-four-more-states/">in North Carolina and Utah</a> over the coming months, and years ago it announced that Kentucky and Mississippi were committed to launching the feature at some point.<br/>
<br/>
To set up the feature, open the Wallet app on the iPhone and tap on the plus sign in the top-right corner. Next, tap on Driver's License and ID Cards, select your state from the list, and follow the on-screen steps to complete the process. Then, you can present your digital ID where it is accepted without handing over your device.<br/>
<br/>
You can present an Apple Wallet ID where accepted by simply tapping your iPhone or Apple Watch on an identity reader. Then, you will be able to view the specific information being requested by the TSA or business. Only after authorizing with Face ID or Touch ID is the requested identity information released from your device.<br/>
<br/>
As mentioned, you do not need to unlock, show, or hand over your device to present an Apple Wallet ID in person, ensuring user privacy.<br/>
<br/>
Apple Wallet IDs are accepted at TSA checkpoints in more than 250 airports across the U.S. for domestic travel, according to Apple.<br/>
<br/>
